The backend in crates/nsh-platform-tizen (in particular its encoding, text,
canvas, effects, animation and FFI modules) started from that project's
crates/nsh-platform-miniprogram. Changes: renamed; a Samsung Tizen TV
environment; remote keys and their routing; a DOM renderer run from a Web
Worker; native components; inputs, images and fonts. Those files say so
in their first line.

The page runtime in runtime/ follows the design of that project's runtime
(runtime/nsh/nsh-mp.js: the module's imports and how strings cross into
it; runtime/nsh/tree.js: applying operations to a tree), rewritten for a
browser page and a Web Worker rather than copied.
